# Architectural Anti-Patterns

Violations of Clean Architecture Dependency Rule and layer structure.

---

## 1. Dependency Rule Violation

**Context:** When analyzing imports between architectural layers. The Dependency Rule states: inner layers must NOT depend on outer layers.

**Forbidden:**

```typescript
// ❌ BAD: Domain importing infrastructure
// src/domain/entities/Usuario.ts
import { store } from '@/app/store'; // Domain knows Redux
import { httpClient } from '@/data/api/httpClient'; // Domain knows HTTP

// ❌ BAD: UseCase importing concrete API
// src/domain/usecases/usuario/ObterUsuarioUseCase.ts
import { usuarioApi } from '@/data/api/usuarioApi'; // UseCase depends on concrete API

// ❌ BAD: Entity knowing implementation details
// src/domain/entities/Feedback.ts
import { firebaseDb } from '@/core/firebase'; // Entity knows Firebase
```

**Required:**

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD: Domain defines interfaces
// src/domain/repositories/UsuarioRepository.ts
export interface UsuarioRepository {
  obterPorId(id: string): Promise<Usuario | null>;
}

// ✅ GOOD: UseCase depends on interface
// src/domain/usecases/usuario/ObterUsuarioUseCase.ts
import type { UsuarioRepository } from '@/domain/repositories/UsuarioRepository';

@injectable()
export class ObterUsuarioUseCase {
  constructor(
    @inject('UsuarioRepository') private repository: UsuarioRepository
  ) {}
  
  async execute(id: string): Promise<Usuario | null> {
    return this.repository.obterPorId(id);
  }
}

// ✅ GOOD: Domain is pure
// src/domain/entities/Feedback.ts
export class Feedback {
  constructor(
    public readonly id: string,
    public readonly comentario: string,
    public readonly nivel: number
  ) {}
  
  // Business logic only, no external dependencies
  validar(): boolean {
    return this.nivel >= 1 && this.nivel <= 5;
  }
}
```

**Impact:**

- Structural coupling - layers become intertwined
- Loss of isolation - can't test layers independently
- Testing difficulty - need to mock infrastructure in domain tests
- Impossibility of implementation swap - can't change data layer without touching domain

**Detection:**

- Look for imports from `app/`, `data/`, `presentation/` in `domain/` files
- Check: `grep -r "from '@\(app\|data\|presentation\)'" src/domain/`
- Forbidden keywords in domain: `Redux`, `fetch`, `axios`, `window`, `document`

