## 4. Layer Cohesion Violation

**Context:** When organizing code or reviewing layer responsibilities. Each layer has one clear responsibility.

**Layer Responsibilities:**

| Layer | Responsibility | Must NOT |
|-------|----------------|----------|
| Presentation | UI rendering, user events | Business logic, API calls |
| App | State management, DI container | Data implementation, business rules |
| Domain | Business rules, entities, use cases | Know HTTP, know React/Redux |
| Data | HTTP calls, repository implementation | Know React, have business logic |
| Shared | Types, constants, generic utilities | Know feature specifics |
| Core | DI container, framework config | Know domain specifics |

**Forbidden:**

```typescript
// ❌ BAD: Business logic in presentation
// src/presentation/pages/recrutamento/GestaoVagas.tsx
const calcularTotal = (itens: Item[]) => {
  // Business calculation should be in domain
  return itens.reduce((sum, item) => sum + item.valor * 1.1, 0);
};

// ❌ BAD: HTTP knowledge in domain
// src/domain/usecases/ProcessarPagamentoUseCase.ts
const response = await fetch('/api/pagamento'); // Domain knows HTTP

// ❌ BAD: React in data layer
// src/data/repositories/VagaRepositoryImpl.ts
import { useSelector } from 'react-redux'; // Data knows React
```

**Required:**

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD: Pure business logic in domain
// src/domain/services/CalculadoraService.ts
export class CalculadoraService {
  static calcularTotal(itens: Item[]): number {
    return itens.reduce((sum, item) => sum + item.valor * 1.1, 0);
  }
}

// ✅ GOOD: UseCase delegates, doesn't implement HTTP
// src/domain/usecases/ProcessarPagamentoUseCase.ts
@injectable()
export class ProcessarPagamentoUseCase {
  constructor(
    @inject('PagamentoRepository') private repo: PagamentoRepository
  ) {}
  
  async execute(dados: ProcessarPagamentoDTO): Promise<Resultado> {
    // Business logic only
    if (!this.validarDados(dados)) {
      throw new ValidationError('Dados invalidos');
    }
    
    // Delegate to repository
    return this.repo.processar(dados);
  }
}

// ✅ GOOD: Page is thin, delegates to domain
// src/presentation/pages/recrutamento/GestaoVagas.tsx
const GestaoVagasPage = () => {
  const container = useContainer();
  const aprovarUseCase = container.resolve(AprovarCandidatoUseCase);
  
  const handleAprovar = async (candidato: Candidato) => {
    const resultado = await aprovarUseCase.execute(candidato.id);
    
    if (resultado.sucesso) {
      toast.success('Candidato aprovado com sucesso');
    } else {
      toast.error(resultado.erro);
    }
  };
};
```

**Impact:**

- Mixed responsibilities - hard to find where things belong
- Unorganized growth - code spreads unpredictably
- Testing difficulty - can't test layers in isolation

**Detection:**

- Business calculations in `.tsx` files (should be in domain/services)
- `fetch`, `axios` in domain or shared
- Redux hooks in data or domain
- Component logic that decides business rules

